    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0603" n="533" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg533"/>

                <head>No. 312.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    West.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-09-28"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 28,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 25th of
                    July last, in relation to the alleged stealing of horses from Canadian territory
                    by South Piegan Indians, and the subsequent correspondence on the subject, I now
                    have the honor to transmit herewith for your information a copy of a report to
                    the Interior Department by the Commissioner of Indian Affairs, from which it
                    appears that twenty of the horses in question have been recovered and delivered
                    to the military authorities, to be turned over to the proper Canadian
                    officers.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d313-a1.xml" xpointer="d313-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
